# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX  # add the Zenodo concept DOI after the first release (see RELEASING.md)
url: "https://aitutorium.com"
repository: "https://github.com/VictorOsondu/ai-adoption-model"
abstract: >-
  A model for AI adoption that sorts people by internal experience rather than
  by tools deployed. Six stages — Nomad, Observer, Dabbler, Integrator,
  Architect, Innovator — each defined by a characteristic feeling and the
  question underneath it. The model's central practitioner claim is that some
  adoption stalls are better explained by identity, confidence, and
  self-permission than by skill gaps alone, most visibly in the transition from
  Integrator to Architect.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - AI adoption
  - change management
  - professional development
  - identity
  - self-efficacy
